            <ArticleTitle>Palliative care pharmacotherapy literature summaries and analyses.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>91-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Timely and important studies are reviewed and commentaries provided by leading palliative care clinicians. Symptoms and treatment side effects addressed in this issue are: cardiovascular risk due to NSAIDs or COX-2 inhibitors; prolongation of the QT interval due to methadone use; depression and its treatment with scopolamine; adverse drug reactions related to cardiovascular medications, and their association with ethnicity; and medication nonadherence in Medicare enrollees due to cost considerations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
